WEBVTT

00:04.924 --> 00:06.891
Oh. Hey.
Hey.

00:06.893 --> 00:08.560
I thought you and Alan
were going out to dinner.

00:08.562 --> 00:10.361
We were supposed to,
but then he discovered

00:10.363 --> 00:12.430
his coupon was only good
for to-go orders.

00:12.432 --> 00:14.799
That guy's a piece of work.

00:14.801 --> 00:15.767
He is.

00:15.769 --> 00:16.968
Which is ironic,

00:16.970 --> 00:19.354
'cause he never seems
to go to work. (laughs)

00:19.356 --> 00:21.573
That's true.

00:21.575 --> 00:22.440
That being said,

00:22.442 --> 00:23.975
I do envy what
you guys have.

00:23.977 --> 00:26.277
You guys are like termites.

00:26.279 --> 00:28.413
Termites?

00:28.415 --> 00:30.314
Yeah, they mate for life,
and once they live

00:30.316 --> 00:31.916
in your house,
you can never get rid of 'em.

00:31.918 --> 00:33.117
(chuckles)

00:33.119 --> 00:36.037
(voice breaking):
Just like Alan.

00:36.039 --> 00:37.372
You all right?

00:37.374 --> 00:39.674
Yeah, I...

00:39.676 --> 00:41.342
I have to do something
with him tonight

00:41.344 --> 00:42.794
that's going to be
really painful.

00:42.796 --> 00:45.430
Okay, that's between
two consenting adults.

00:45.432 --> 00:47.465
No...

00:47.467 --> 00:49.000
(sighs)

00:49.002 --> 00:50.552
I'm breaking up
with him.

00:50.554 --> 00:52.336
What?

00:53.439 --> 00:55.890
No, but you guys are great
together.

00:55.892 --> 00:58.643
You're so beautiful

00:58.645 --> 01:00.945
and smart and fun and...

01:00.947 --> 01:03.231
Alan's so...

01:03.233 --> 01:04.515
lucky.

01:05.701 --> 01:07.819
I don't want
to hurt him.

01:07.821 --> 01:10.038
Then do something else.

01:10.040 --> 01:12.189
Disneyland, dancing, bowling,

01:12.191 --> 01:14.075
pretty much anything
but break up with him.

01:14.077 --> 01:15.493
I have to.

01:15.495 --> 01:17.412
But you and I are his world.

01:17.414 --> 01:19.380
And if you leave,
I'll be his world.

01:19.382 --> 01:20.715
I'm sorry.

01:20.717 --> 01:22.216
No, I don't think
you heard me.

01:22.218 --> 01:24.385
I'll. Be. His. World.

01:24.387 --> 01:27.255
(crying):
I feel so bad.

01:27.257 --> 01:28.306
(sobbing)

01:28.308 --> 01:30.041
All right.

01:30.043 --> 01:31.209
Come here.

01:33.178 --> 01:36.314
This is the hardest thing
I've ever had to do.

01:36.316 --> 01:38.983
And I pushed a baby
out of my vagina.

01:38.985 --> 01:40.151
(sobbing)

01:40.153 --> 01:42.020
ALAN:
I'm back!

01:42.022 --> 01:43.071
(gasps, sniffs)

01:43.073 --> 01:45.056
Don't say anything.

01:45.058 --> 01:47.442
Oh. Hey, Walden.
Want to join us?

01:47.444 --> 01:50.361
Uh... no, thanks.

01:50.363 --> 01:53.031
Hey, what do you say
we all go bowling?

01:53.033 --> 01:54.732
Huh?

01:54.734 --> 01:56.167
Doesn't that sound fun?

01:56.169 --> 01:57.702
Just bowling?

01:57.704 --> 02:00.571
No, I... I think we're
just gonna stay in tonight.

02:00.573 --> 02:02.573
Uh... oh, but I have
a confession to make.

02:02.575 --> 02:05.076
I, uh, opened my fortune
cookie in the car...

02:05.078 --> 02:06.427
and listen to this:

02:06.429 --> 02:09.547
uh... "your life is about to
take a turn for the better."

02:13.886 --> 02:17.355
I think you may have gotten
Lyndsey's cookie.

02:18.974 --> 02:21.893
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

02:21.895 --> 02:25.029
♪ Men, men, men, manly men, men ♪
♪ Ooh

02:25.031 --> 02:28.265
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men ♪
♪ Ooh

02:28.267 --> 02:30.401
♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh,
ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh... ♪

02:30.403 --> 02:32.870
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

02:32.872 --> 02:36.658
♪ Ooh
♪ Men, men, men, manly men, men, men ♪

02:36.660 --> 02:40.795
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.

02:40.820 --> 02:44.820
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 10x21 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Another Night With Neil Diamond&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on April 25, 2013

02:44.845 --> 02:49.845
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

02:51.647 --> 02:52.780
Would you like another
glass of wi...?

02:52.782 --> 02:53.948
Yes.

03:01.824 --> 03:03.324
Oh, you know,
I was thinking, uh...

03:03.326 --> 03:05.727
after dinner we could
light a fire.

03:05.729 --> 03:07.829
Don't worry, I've got all
the wood we'll need.

03:15.170 --> 03:17.338
Cute.

03:17.340 --> 03:20.074
Just, uh... you seem
awfully quiet tonight.

03:20.076 --> 03:21.109
Is everything okay?

03:21.111 --> 03:23.478
I-I've just got
a lot on my mind.

03:23.480 --> 03:25.480
Hmm, what is it,
sweetie?

03:25.482 --> 03:27.482
Oh, boy.

03:27.484 --> 03:28.716
I don't know
how to say this.

03:28.718 --> 03:31.552
Well, a problem shared is
a problem halved.

03:31.554 --> 03:33.688
It's kind of like
that fried rice,

03:33.690 --> 03:35.390
although I noticed
you didn't touch your half,

03:35.392 --> 03:37.458
despite the fact
that you had to order it,

03:37.460 --> 03:38.927
even though
the white rice is free

03:38.929 --> 03:42.030
and the coupon specifically
said "no substitutions."

03:42.032 --> 03:44.332
I think we should break up.

03:45.935 --> 03:47.068
Excuse me.

03:51.740 --> 03:53.308
Are you okay?

04:10.626 --> 04:12.827
You owe me $22.50 for dinner.

04:15.280 --> 04:16.614
Hey, Berta.

04:16.616 --> 04:18.833
Just finishing up.
Then I'll get out of your way.

04:18.835 --> 04:20.551
No, I think
you should stay here.

04:20.553 --> 04:22.003
All right.

04:22.005 --> 04:24.138
Let me take
a quick shower first.

04:24.140 --> 04:26.007
No.

04:26.009 --> 04:28.309
Lyndsey's downstairs breaking up
with Alan.

04:28.311 --> 04:29.427
Really?

04:29.429 --> 04:30.478
Yeah.

04:30.480 --> 04:33.765
Well... we knew this was coming.

04:33.767 --> 04:35.516
First time I saw them together,

04:35.518 --> 04:36.851
I asked her to blink twice

04:36.853 --> 04:38.803
if she was being held hostage.

04:38.805 --> 04:41.239
He's gonna be devastated.

04:42.491 --> 04:43.825
I mean, he's madly
in love with her,

04:43.827 --> 04:44.826
they've been dating for years,

04:44.828 --> 04:46.194
they were planning
on getting married.

04:46.196 --> 04:48.946
Oh, my God,
he's never gonna leave my house.

04:48.948 --> 04:52.834
It's sweet that you actually
thought he was going to.

04:52.836 --> 04:54.686
Why do people have to break up?

04:54.688 --> 04:56.421
Well, in my experience,

04:56.423 --> 04:58.122
either the magic wears off,

04:58.124 --> 04:59.624
or the mushrooms.

05:02.094 --> 05:03.594
I feel really bad for him.

05:03.596 --> 05:05.213
I mean,
I always feel bad for him.

05:05.215 --> 05:07.382
But I feel &lt;i>really&lt;/i> bad for him.

05:07.384 --> 05:08.800
Yeah, yeah. It's tough.

05:08.802 --> 05:11.502
We gonna do this thing
or what?

05:16.058 --> 05:18.059
I don't understand.
Where is this coming from?

05:18.061 --> 05:19.944
There's no spark anymore.

05:19.946 --> 05:21.779
All we do is sit around,
watch TV and eat takeout

05:21.781 --> 05:23.731
from whatever restaurant
you have a coupon for.

05:23.733 --> 05:25.199
Did you want to go
to the food court?

05:25.201 --> 05:26.234
'Cause we can do that.

05:26.236 --> 05:28.653
Alan, it's not that.

05:28.655 --> 05:29.871
Then, what is it?

05:29.873 --> 05:31.406
I mean, I-I...
I thought you were happy.

05:31.408 --> 05:32.623
I-I thought
everything was great.

05:32.625 --> 05:35.192
It was, but, but things
change, people change.

05:35.194 --> 05:37.045
That's not true.
I don't change. I never change.

05:37.047 --> 05:39.630
Maybe that's part
of the problem.

05:39.632 --> 05:41.198
I can change.

05:41.200 --> 05:42.834
I-I know this is upsetting,

05:42.836 --> 05:45.536
but, but better to do this
now before it gets worse.

05:45.538 --> 05:46.888
How can it be worse?

05:46.890 --> 05:48.389
You gonna tell me you've been
faking it all these years?

05:48.391 --> 05:49.507
Don't answer that.

05:51.260 --> 05:52.310
Alan, I have to go.

05:52.312 --> 05:53.261
Fine, go.

05:53.263 --> 05:55.563
Don't go.

05:55.565 --> 05:57.682
I-I'm really sorry.

05:57.684 --> 06:00.435
The thing is, I-I
still love you, Alan.

06:01.854 --> 06:04.221
I'm just not in love
with you anymore.

06:08.610 --> 06:10.695
It's not a deal-breaker.

06:13.916 --> 06:15.733
You okay?

06:15.735 --> 06:17.735
I guess.

06:17.737 --> 06:20.004
I suppose it's better that
she broke up with me now

06:20.006 --> 06:22.039
than after we got married.

06:22.041 --> 06:25.293
Then she would've gotten
half of all my stuff.

06:30.532 --> 06:32.633
Sure.

06:34.636 --> 06:37.254
You know I'm
here for you.

06:37.256 --> 06:40.224
I know that and,
and I appreciate it.

06:40.226 --> 06:42.360
But... I'm good.

06:42.362 --> 06:43.561
Good.

06:45.514 --> 06:47.165
Walden?

06:47.167 --> 06:48.366
Yeah?

06:49.151 --> 06:51.101
(sobbing):
I'm not good.

06:51.103 --> 06:53.404
I love her.

06:53.406 --> 06:54.772
(sobbing)

06:54.774 --> 06:55.907
I know you do.

06:55.909 --> 06:58.242
I'll never find another one
like her.

06:58.244 --> 07:00.378
I know you won't.

07:02.915 --> 07:05.666
I-I'm just saying, I-I
know how great she is.

07:05.668 --> 07:07.051
(grunts)
You're gonna be fine.

07:07.053 --> 07:09.620
Just... you have to focus on
the good things in your life.

07:09.622 --> 07:12.890
Lyndsey was the only
good thing in my life.

07:12.892 --> 07:14.976
(sobbing): Oh, God...
It's okay.

07:14.978 --> 07:16.961
(sobbing loudly)
Let it all out.

07:16.963 --> 07:17.979
(Alan wails)

07:17.981 --> 07:20.148
(sobbing noisily)

07:22.968 --> 07:26.070
That's a lot out.
Let's-let's put some back in.

07:26.072 --> 07:29.774
(Alan wails)

07:29.776 --> 07:32.810
Now you're all I have!

07:32.812 --> 07:34.996
(Alan sobbing)

07:41.954 --> 07:44.121
(Walden sobbing)

07:45.707 --> 07:47.959
(sobbing):
I know.

07:52.181 --> 07:53.431
Good morning.

07:53.433 --> 07:55.299
Beautiful day.

07:55.301 --> 07:57.351
To... stick your head
in an oven?

07:59.021 --> 08:01.439
Okay, I realize I was a
little upset last night.

08:01.441 --> 08:02.773
A little?

08:02.775 --> 08:05.175
You Googled "how to kill
yourself without it hurting."

08:05.177 --> 08:07.044
(singsongy):
Drama queen.

08:07.046 --> 08:09.080
But I woke up
this morning

08:09.082 --> 08:11.148
and I realized, "What
am I so upset about?"

08:11.150 --> 08:13.017
Lyndsey and I are
not breaking up.

08:14.703 --> 08:16.254
Okay.

08:16.256 --> 08:19.957
So, when she said that she
didn't want to see you anymore

08:19.959 --> 08:22.310
and she didn't think you made
a good couple

08:22.312 --> 08:23.844
and she wasn't in love with you,
that...

08:23.846 --> 08:24.996
What do you call that?

08:24.998 --> 08:27.698
Foreplay.

08:27.700 --> 08:30.367
Okay. Looks like someone's
starting the day

08:30.369 --> 08:32.720
with a hot, steaming cup
of denial.

08:32.722 --> 08:35.306
No, no, no. This is a little
dance we do all the time.

08:35.308 --> 08:37.141
She decides that
I did something wrong

08:37.143 --> 08:38.409
and gives me the business,

08:38.411 --> 08:39.577
and then I apologize,

08:39.579 --> 08:41.279
and I give her the business.

08:44.149 --> 08:45.733
Okay, see, that right there?

08:45.735 --> 08:47.685
That's why she broke up
with you.

08:47.687 --> 08:49.820
I'm telling you,
we are not broken up.

08:49.822 --> 08:52.189
Okay, I see what
you're doing here,

08:52.191 --> 08:54.792
but pretending like what
happened didn't happen

08:54.794 --> 08:56.027
won't make it not happen,

08:56.029 --> 08:59.363
no matter what you would like
to have had happened.

08:59.365 --> 09:01.198
Yeah, that's right.

09:01.200 --> 09:03.951
Well, thank you,
I appreciate it.

09:03.953 --> 09:06.420
But if you'll excuse me,
I'm gonna go get my girl back.

09:06.422 --> 09:07.939
Okay.

09:07.941 --> 09:10.174
Just in case,
I'll preheat the oven.

09:13.645 --> 09:15.813
(doorbell rings)

09:17.749 --> 09:19.817
Alan?

09:19.819 --> 09:21.218
What are you doing here?

09:21.220 --> 09:23.304
What am I doing here?

09:23.306 --> 09:24.722
That's what I love about you.

09:24.724 --> 09:26.057
Okay, let's do this.

09:26.059 --> 09:28.476
I'm sorry.

09:30.395 --> 09:32.596
There's nothing
to be sorry about.

09:32.598 --> 09:34.365
Our relationship just
isn't going anywhere.

09:34.367 --> 09:37.201
All right, all right. Message
received, loud and clear.

09:37.203 --> 09:38.653
Now let's get down to bidness.

09:40.355 --> 09:42.707
Alan, it's over.

09:42.709 --> 09:44.108
But... but why?

09:44.110 --> 09:46.294
I-It just is.

09:46.296 --> 09:48.212
Is it because we don't
like the same things?

09:48.214 --> 09:50.414
'Cause I can learn
to love sports.

09:50.416 --> 09:51.949
It has nothing
to do with that...

09:51.951 --> 09:53.250
Is it, is it
because I'm-I'm frugal?

09:53.252 --> 09:54.502
'Cause okay, watch this.

09:54.504 --> 09:58.139
I am going to rip a twent--
a five-dollar bill in half.

09:58.141 --> 09:59.340
Okay?

10:00.592 --> 10:03.094
Tell me that's not sexy.

10:03.096 --> 10:05.629
Okay, look... (sighs)

10:05.631 --> 10:07.315
I didn't want
to have to say this,

10:07.317 --> 10:10.935
but the fact of the matter is...

10:10.937 --> 10:11.936
I've met someone else.

10:11.938 --> 10:13.688
Oh. Wow.

10:13.690 --> 10:14.972
Wow. Uh...

10:14.974 --> 10:17.158
World spinning,
uh, gut tightening,

10:17.160 --> 10:18.993
vomit rising... um...

10:18.995 --> 10:20.711
I'm really sorry.

10:20.713 --> 10:22.330
Well, well, who is he?
What's the difference?

10:22.332 --> 10:24.832
Well, I-I need to know
who my competition is.

10:24.834 --> 10:26.334
I-I need to know how I can win.

10:26.336 --> 10:28.669
You can't win.

10:28.671 --> 10:29.754
Good-bye, Alan.

10:29.756 --> 10:31.856
(laughing)

10:31.858 --> 10:33.924
Well, I have got
news for you.

10:33.926 --> 10:37.011
The word "win" is not
in my vocabular...

10:37.013 --> 10:38.095
"Can't."

10:38.097 --> 10:40.931
The word "can't" is not
in my vocabulary.

10:40.933 --> 10:42.633
Damn it.

10:42.635 --> 10:43.701
(screams)

10:43.703 --> 10:45.836
Son of a bitch!

10:45.838 --> 10:46.804
(kicks)

10:46.806 --> 10:49.056
(screams)

10:52.644 --> 10:54.678
Of course.

10:54.680 --> 10:56.881
Dog crap.

11:08.093 --> 11:10.378
(grunts)

11:10.380 --> 11:13.547
Hey, there's soup on the stove
if you want some.

11:13.549 --> 11:16.651
I wonder if Lyndsey's
new boyfriend likes soup.

11:16.653 --> 11:19.070
He probably loves soup.

11:19.072 --> 11:21.422
And wears cable knit sweaters.

11:21.424 --> 11:23.441
"Look at me,
I'm eating soup

11:23.443 --> 11:26.027
"and wearing a sweater
while I bang the memory

11:26.029 --> 11:27.912
of Alan Harper
out of this woman's mind."

11:27.914 --> 11:32.283
(fake chuckles)

11:34.169 --> 11:35.836
Alan, let it go.

11:35.838 --> 11:36.871
You brought it up.

11:36.873 --> 11:38.623
I brought up soup.

11:39.541 --> 11:41.759
I can't stop thinking about him.

11:41.761 --> 11:44.645
And her...
and what they're doing.

11:44.647 --> 11:47.265
And what position
they're doing it in.

11:47.267 --> 11:48.916
And where they're doing it.

11:48.918 --> 11:51.636
In the bed, in the shower,
at the Costco

11:51.638 --> 11:54.755
between the meat and the tires.
That was our place!

11:54.757 --> 11:57.708
That shouldn't be
anyone's place.

11:59.111 --> 12:00.978
And you're obsessing.
No, I'm not.

12:00.980 --> 12:03.097
Right, we all picture
our exes screwing

12:03.099 --> 12:05.149
between a rump roast
and a snow tire.

12:05.151 --> 12:07.652
You know what,
I-I'm gonna go for a drive.

12:07.654 --> 12:08.769
Where?

12:08.771 --> 12:10.571
Just out, you know, joyride.

12:10.573 --> 12:13.541
I've seen your car,
there's no joy in that ride.

12:15.110 --> 12:16.994
Now where are you going?
I'm just gonna drive

12:16.996 --> 12:19.247
up the coast a little bit.
Take in the sea air.

12:19.249 --> 12:21.465
How? Your windows
don't roll down.

12:21.467 --> 12:23.834
Just the ones in the front. The
ones in the back don't roll up.

12:23.836 --> 12:25.553
Good-bye.

12:26.388 --> 12:28.673
I should buy him a new car.

12:28.675 --> 12:31.058
So he can live in it.

12:32.811 --> 12:34.512
♪ Men

12:34.514 --> 12:36.013
All right.

12:36.015 --> 12:37.848
Where are they?

12:37.850 --> 12:42.153
(sighs) They're probably
watching sports right now.

12:42.155 --> 12:44.972
"Hello, Lyndsey,
you don't mind if I watch

12:44.974 --> 12:48.475
"this baseball game
in the nude, do you?

12:48.477 --> 12:51.529
"Sure, you can kiss me
between the strikes

12:51.531 --> 12:54.365
and I'll kiss you
between the balls."

12:54.367 --> 12:56.117
(phone rings)

12:57.452 --> 13:00.121
Oh.

13:00.123 --> 13:01.756
Hey, Walden.

13:01.758 --> 13:03.674
Yeah, I'm just, uh,
you know, taking a drive

13:03.676 --> 13:06.544
down the Malibu coast,
trying to clear my head.

13:06.546 --> 13:08.846
Yeah, now I'm, uh,
I'm walking on the beach.

13:08.848 --> 13:10.798
Sand feels nice on my toesies.

13:10.800 --> 13:13.184
(pounding)
(screams)

13:16.054 --> 13:17.338
Walking on the beach, huh?

13:17.340 --> 13:18.522
Are you stalking me?

13:18.524 --> 13:19.774
Are you stalking Lyndsey?

13:19.776 --> 13:21.659
I asked you first.

13:21.661 --> 13:22.743
Look, this
is pathetic.

13:22.745 --> 13:23.861
Sitting outside
a woman's house,

13:23.863 --> 13:25.946
trying to catch of glimpse
of her through the window.

13:25.948 --> 13:27.448
What kind
of person does that?

13:27.450 --> 13:29.850
(pounding)
(both scream)

13:30.702 --> 13:33.037
Hey, guys, what are we doing?

13:33.039 --> 13:35.323
Playing a little peek-a-boo
with Lyndsey?

13:35.325 --> 13:36.540
No.

13:36.542 --> 13:38.492
Yes.

13:38.494 --> 13:39.794
Lyndsey broke
up with Alan

13:39.796 --> 13:41.295
and he's having a hard
time understanding.

13:41.297 --> 13:42.997
Oh, well, one look
at the new guy

13:42.999 --> 13:43.998
and you'd understand it.

13:44.000 --> 13:46.417
What, you've seen him?
Oh, yeah.

13:46.419 --> 13:47.335
Nick's gorgeous.

13:47.337 --> 13:48.469
Kind of looks like Walden.

13:48.471 --> 13:49.920
Aw, thank you.

13:49.922 --> 13:52.673
Y-You know his name,
so you-you've met him?

13:52.675 --> 13:54.475
Well, no,
but I've heard her yell it.

13:54.477 --> 13:57.144
It's either Nick
or Oh, God, Right There.

13:58.230 --> 14:00.047
Oh, that's it.

14:00.049 --> 14:02.216
I got to see this Nick guy
for myself.

14:03.268 --> 14:05.552
No, Alan, don't.

14:05.554 --> 14:07.271
You're better than this.

14:07.273 --> 14:09.407
We both know
that's not true!

14:10.392 --> 14:13.444
Yeah, I feel for him.
It's got to be tough.

14:13.446 --> 14:15.562
Yeah, no doubt.

14:15.564 --> 14:18.032
You really are
a very handsome man.

14:18.034 --> 14:20.567
Again... thank you.

14:20.569 --> 14:24.588
It's not hard to imagine you
naked and cast in marble.

14:26.525 --> 14:28.909
Getting weird, Herb.

14:28.911 --> 14:30.878
Right.

14:35.750 --> 14:37.768
All right.

14:37.770 --> 14:39.103
Where are you, you homewrecker?

14:39.105 --> 14:41.389
(crackling)
Oh...

14:46.061 --> 14:48.762
(panting)

14:51.366 --> 14:53.317
That's better.

14:53.319 --> 14:55.636
(owl hoots)

14:55.638 --> 14:56.904
(screams)

14:56.906 --> 14:59.123
(thud)
Ugh.

15:00.625 --> 15:03.160
Can this get any worse?

15:03.162 --> 15:07.114
LYNDSEY:
Oh, God, Nick, right there!

15:07.116 --> 15:09.783
ALAN:
Aw.

15:12.087 --> 15:15.089
(beeping)

15:15.091 --> 15:16.140
Lyndsey,

15:16.142 --> 15:17.391
hey.

15:17.393 --> 15:18.442
Hey,

15:18.444 --> 15:19.677
I need your help.

15:19.679 --> 15:22.430
You need my help getting
back together with Alan?

15:22.432 --> 15:25.599
No. I need you to tell him
to stop calling, e-mailing,

15:25.601 --> 15:26.600
and texting me.

15:26.602 --> 15:27.968
Words and pictures.

15:27.970 --> 15:29.603
Especially the pictures.

15:30.472 --> 15:32.907
He's just upset.
He means well.

15:32.909 --> 15:34.608
Really?
Does this picture look

15:34.610 --> 15:35.810
like he means well?

15:35.812 --> 15:38.412
Oh, dear God.

15:38.414 --> 15:42.016
Is he lying on my kitchen table?

15:42.018 --> 15:43.984
So, will you talk to him?

15:43.986 --> 15:48.005
Sure, right after I burn
my kitchen table.

15:48.007 --> 15:52.659
Thank you. By the way, you might
want to burn your bathtub, too.

15:52.661 --> 15:53.677
(Alan grunting)

15:53.679 --> 15:55.679
Oh, he's coming now.
Got to go.

15:55.681 --> 15:58.098
(grunting)

15:58.967 --> 16:02.303
Hey. There he is.

16:02.305 --> 16:04.972
Looking good.

16:04.974 --> 16:07.024
Ha-ha.

16:07.026 --> 16:09.109
(grunts)

16:09.111 --> 16:10.728
Where you going?

16:10.730 --> 16:13.013
Lyndsey un-friended me
on Facebook.

16:13.015 --> 16:16.317
So I'm going to go
re-friend her with my face.

16:16.319 --> 16:17.918
No, you're not.

16:17.920 --> 16:19.520
You can't stop me.

16:28.863 --> 16:31.565
Damn you.

16:36.888 --> 16:38.372
(knocking)

16:38.374 --> 16:40.057
Hey, Zip.

16:40.059 --> 16:41.842
Oh, what do you want?

16:41.844 --> 16:45.846
A motorcycle and another night
with Neil Diamond.

16:45.848 --> 16:48.315
But for now we need to talk.

16:48.317 --> 16:50.267
I just want to be left alone.

16:50.269 --> 16:53.070
Like I'm gonna be
for the rest of my life.

16:53.072 --> 16:55.389
Look, Lyndsey's crazy
for breaking up with you.

16:55.391 --> 16:56.941
You are a great guy.

16:56.943 --> 16:58.158
You're just saying that.

16:58.160 --> 16:59.610
I know I'm rough on you,

16:59.612 --> 17:00.778
but that's just for fun.

17:00.780 --> 17:03.080
I really mean this.

17:03.082 --> 17:05.282
Oh, thank you.

17:05.284 --> 17:07.668
All right,
good talk.

17:07.670 --> 17:09.069
How?

17:09.071 --> 17:10.588
What?

17:10.590 --> 17:12.906
How am I a great guy?

17:12.908 --> 17:16.176
(sighs)

17:16.178 --> 17:19.246
Well, you're
punctual.

17:19.248 --> 17:21.748
I-I do make it
a priority to be on time.

17:21.750 --> 17:23.267
Yep.

17:23.269 --> 17:25.052
What else?

17:25.054 --> 17:28.022
(sighs)

17:28.024 --> 17:29.440
Okay.

17:29.442 --> 17:32.810
You have pretty good toilet aim.

17:32.812 --> 17:35.729
And that's important
to a housekeeper.

17:35.731 --> 17:38.532
My secret is, I sit down.

17:39.384 --> 17:41.368
And that should've
stayed a secret.

17:41.370 --> 17:42.786
Take care.

17:42.788 --> 17:44.204
Berta?

17:44.206 --> 17:47.324
(sighs)
What?

17:47.326 --> 17:49.727
I-I-If I'm such
a great guy,

17:49.729 --> 17:52.246
then why did
Lyndsey leave me?

17:52.248 --> 17:54.448
Oh, there's no telling
with chicks.

17:54.450 --> 17:57.918
But don't worry...
you'll find somebody else.

17:57.920 --> 17:59.253
As good as Lyndsey?

17:59.255 --> 18:00.421
(chuckles)

18:00.423 --> 18:04.592
Look at you,
already making jokes.

18:08.013 --> 18:09.463
How'd it go?

18:09.465 --> 18:11.465
He's gonna die alone.

18:11.467 --> 18:13.467
And he pees sitting down.

18:17.939 --> 18:20.974
I really don't want
to be here, Walden.

18:20.976 --> 18:22.192
What are you
talking about?

18:22.194 --> 18:23.360
You're doing great.

18:23.362 --> 18:25.746
You shaved,
you showered.

18:25.748 --> 18:27.615
You realized wearing
Lyndsey's underwear

18:27.617 --> 18:30.451
wasn't a
long-term solution.

18:30.453 --> 18:32.319
I may have it together
on the outside,

18:32.321 --> 18:33.987
but on the inside
I'm still a wreck.

18:33.989 --> 18:36.707
I just want to go home and
eat ice cream on the toilet

18:36.709 --> 18:37.824
until I fall asleep.

18:37.826 --> 18:40.327
Would you listen
to yourself?

18:40.329 --> 18:42.596
Trust me, tonight
is going to be fun.

18:42.598 --> 18:45.165
Okay. But if it's not,
you're gonna have to watch

18:45.167 --> 18:46.500
&lt;i>The Notebook&lt;/i> with me.

18:46.502 --> 18:48.835
Really? Again?

18:49.688 --> 18:51.388
WOMAN:
Walden.

18:51.390 --> 18:53.774
Oh, hey, Allie, hi.

18:53.776 --> 18:56.276
This is, uh, my friend Alan
I was telling you about.

18:56.278 --> 18:57.277
Hi, Alan.

18:57.279 --> 18:58.278
Hello.

18:58.280 --> 18:59.980
You two have
a lot in common.

18:59.982 --> 19:01.398
Really?

19:01.400 --> 19:03.484
You know your girlfriend's
new boyfriend, Nick?

19:03.486 --> 19:04.518
Yeah.

19:04.520 --> 19:06.654
I'm his
soon-to-be ex-wife.

19:07.389 --> 19:09.873
I'll just
let you two talk.

19:09.875 --> 19:12.087
Oh, oh... you know, I-I

19:12.112 --> 19:14.463
can see what Walden's
trying to do here,

19:14.464 --> 19:17.464
and he means well,
but, um, I-I don't know

19:17.466 --> 19:18.865
that I'm emotionally
ready to jump

19:18.867 --> 19:20.701
back into the relation...
How do you feel about revenge sex?

19:20.703 --> 19:22.002
Big fan. I'll
get the check.

19:35.048 --> 19:37.183
Well, well, well.

19:37.185 --> 19:39.735
Look who's doing
the walk of shame.

19:39.737 --> 19:42.154
More like the stride of pride.

19:43.223 --> 19:45.441
Guess who heard
"Oh, God, right there"

19:45.443 --> 19:47.827
multiple times last night?

19:47.829 --> 19:48.894
Not Nick.

19:48.896 --> 19:50.412
Well,
congratulations.

19:50.414 --> 19:52.014
I'm very happy
for you.

19:52.016 --> 19:54.250
I have you to thank you it.
Ah, I didn't do anything.

19:54.252 --> 19:56.619
Well, tracking Allie down
couldn't have been easy.

19:56.621 --> 19:57.736
It wasn't that hard.

19:57.738 --> 19:59.088
When we were
outside Lyndsey's house,

19:59.090 --> 20:01.040
she was parked right behind us.

20:02.042 --> 20:04.510
Which is ironic,
because last night I was parked

20:04.512 --> 20:07.680
behind her...
I got it, I got it.

20:07.682 --> 20:09.798
I'm happy you're
feeling better.

20:09.800 --> 20:10.983
Oh, yeah.

20:10.985 --> 20:13.819
And let me tell you,
revenge sex is way better

20:13.821 --> 20:16.138
than revenge masturbation.

20:18.825 --> 20:22.561
Course, there's no reason
you can't do both.

20:27.034 --> 20:28.969
Oh, God, why am I eating
on this table?

20:28.971 --> 20:33.971
